{
  "title": "53: al-Najm النجم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالنَّجْمِ اِذَا هَوٰىۙ‏(1)\n\nBy the star when it sets:\nمَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمْ وَمَا غَوٰى‌ۚ‏(2)\n\nyour companion has neither gone astray, nor amiss.\nوَمَا يَنْطِقُ عَنِ الْهَوٰىؕ‏(3)\n\nNor does he speak out of [his own] desire:\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا وَحْىٌ يُّوْحٰىۙ‏(4)\n\nit is just a revelation that is revealed [to him],\nعَلَّمَهٗ شَدِيْدُ الْقُوٰىۙ‏(5)\n\ntaught him by one of great powers,\nذُوْ مِرَّةٍؕ فَاسْتَوٰىۙ‏(6)\n\npossessed of sound judgement. He settled,\nوَهُوَ بِالْاُفُقِ الْاَعْلٰى ؕ‏(7)\n\nwhile he was on the highest horizon.\nثُمَّ دَنَا فَتَدَلّٰىۙ‏(8)\n\nThen he drew nearer and nearer\nفَكَانَ قَابَ قَوْسَيْنِ اَوْ اَدْنٰى‌ۚ‏(9)\n\nuntil he was within two bows’ length or even nearer,\nفَاَوْحٰۤى الٰى عَبْدِهٖ مَاۤ اَوْحٰىؕ‏(10)\n\nwhereat He revealed to His servant whatever He revealed.\nمَا كَذَبَ الْفُؤَادُ مَا رَاٰى‏(11)\n\nThe heart did not deny what it saw.\nاَفَتُمٰرُوْنَهٗ عَلٰى مَا يَرٰى‏(12)\n\nWill you then dispute with him about what he saw?!\nوَلَقَدْ رَاٰهُ نَزْلَةً اُخْرٰىۙ‏(13)\n\nCertainly he saw it yet another time,\nعِنْدَ سِدْرَةِ الْمُنْتَهٰى‏(14)\n\nby the Lote Tree of the Ultimate Boundary,\nعِنْدَهَا جَنَّةُ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(15)\n\nnear which is the Garden of the Abode,\nاِذْ يَغْشَى السِّدْرَةَ مَا يَغْشٰىۙ‏(16)\n\nwhen there covered the Lote Tree what covered it.\nمَا زَاغَ الْبَصَرُ وَمَا طَغٰى‏(17)\n\nHis gaze did not swerve, nor did it overstep the bounds.\nلَقَدْ رَاٰى مِنْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِ الْكُبْرٰى‏(18)\n\nCertainly he saw some of the greatest signs of his Lord.\nاَفَرَءَيْتُمُ اللّٰتَ وَالْعُزّٰىۙ‏(19)\n\nHave you considered Lat and ‘Uzza?\nوَمَنٰوةَ الثَّالِثَةَ الْاُخْرٰى‏(20)\n\nand Manat, the third one?\nاَلَكُمُ الذَّكَرُ وَلَهُ الْاُنْثٰى‏(21)\n\nAre you to have males and He females?\nتِلْكَ اِذًا قِسْمَةٌ ضِيْزٰى‏(22)\n\nThat, then, will be an unfair division!\nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَآءٌ سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهْوَى الْاَنْفُسُ‌ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمُ الْهُدٰىؕ‏(23)\n\nThese are but names, which you have coined—you and your fathers—for which Allah has not sent down any authority. They follow nothing but conjectures and the desires of the [lower] soul, while there has already come to them the guidance from their Lord.\nاَمْ لِلْاِنْسَانِ مَا تَمَنّٰى   ۖ‏(24)\n\nShall man have whatever he yearns for?\nفَلِلّٰهِ الْاٰخِرَةُ وَالْاُوْلٰى‏(25)\n\nYet to Allah belong this world and the Hereafter.\nوَكَمْ مِّنْ مَّلَكٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ لَا تُغْنِىْ شَفَاعَتُهُمْ شَيْئًا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَنْ يَّاْذَنَ اللّٰهُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَرْضٰى‏(26)\n\nHow many an angel there is in the heavens whose intercession is of not any avail, except after Allah permits whomever He wishes and approves of!\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ لَيُسَمُّوْنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ تَسْمِيَةَ الْاُنْثٰى‏(27)\n\nIndeed those who do not believe in the Hereafter give female names to the angels.\nوَمَا لَهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ‌ۚ وَاِنَّ الظَّنَّ لَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ شَيْئًاۚ‏(28)\n\nThey do not have any knowledge of that. They follow nothing but conjectures, and conjecture is no substitute for the truth.\nفَاَعْرِضْ عَنْ مَّنْ تَوَلّٰى ۙ عَنْ ذِكْرِنَا وَلَمْ يُرِدْ اِلَّا الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ؕ‏(29)\n\nSo avoid those who turn away from Our remembrance and desire nothing but the life of the world.\nذٰ لِكَ مَبْلَغُهُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ ضَلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ۙ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اهْتَدٰى‏(30)\n\nThat is the ultimate reach of their knowledge. Indeed your Lord knows best those who stray from His way, and He knows best those who are [rightly] guided.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِۙ لِيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسَآءُوْا بِمَا عَمِلُوْا وَيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا بِالْحُسْنٰى‌ ۚ‏(31)\n\nTo Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, that He may requite those who do evil for what they have done, and reward those who do good with the best [of rewards].\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَجْتَنِبُوْنَ كَبٰٓئِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَالْفوَاحِشَ اِلَّا اللَّمَمَ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ وَاسِعُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‌ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْ اِذْ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاِذْ اَنْتُمْ اَجِنَّةٌ فِىْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ‌ۚ فَلَا تُزَكُّوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ‌ ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اتَّقٰى‏(32)\n\nThose who avoid major sins and indecencies, apart from [minor and occasional] lapses. Indeed your Lord is expansive in [His] forgiveness. He knows you best since [the time] He produced you from the earth and since you were foetuses in the bellies of your mothers. So do not flaunt your piety: He knows best those who are Godwary.\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ تَوَلّٰىۙ‏(33)\n\nDid you see him who turned away,\nوَاَعْطٰى قَلِيْلًا وَّاَكْدٰى‏(34)\n\ngave a little and held off?\nاَعِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ الْغَيْبِ فَهُوَ يَرٰى‏(35)\n\nDoes he have the knowledge of the Unseen so that he sees?\nاَمْ لَمْ يُنَبَّاْ بِمَا فِىْ صُحُفِ مُوْسٰىۙ‏(36)\n\nHas he not been informed of what is in the scriptures of Moses,\nوَاِبْرٰهِيْمَ الَّذِىْ وَفّٰىٓ  ۙ‏(37)\n\nand of Abraham, who fulfilled [his summons]:\nاَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰىۙ‏(38)\n\nthat no bearer shall bear another’s burden,\nوَاَنْ لَّيْسَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ اِلَّا مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(39)\n\nthat nothing belongs to man except what he strives for,\nوَاَنَّ سَعْيَهٗ سَوْفَ يُرٰى‏(40)\n\nand that he will soon be shown his endeavour,\nثُمَّ يُجْزٰٮهُ الْجَزَآءَ الْاَوْفٰىۙ‏(41)\n\nthen he will be rewarded for it with the fullest reward;\nوَاَنَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ الْمُنْتَهٰىۙ‏(42)\n\nthat the terminus is toward your Lord,\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَضْحَكَ وَاَبْكٰىۙ‏(43)\n\nthat it is He who makes [men] laugh, and weep,\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَمَاتَ وَ اَحْيَا ۙ‏(44)\n\nthat it is He who brings death and gives life,\nوَاَنَّهٗ خَلَقَ الزَّوْجَيْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰىۙ‏(45)\n\nthat it is He who created the mates, the male and the female,\nمِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ اِذَا تُمْنٰى‏(46)\n\nfrom a drop of [seminal] fluid when emitted;\nوَاَنَّ عَلَيْهِ النَّشْاَةَ الْاُخْرٰىۙ‏(47)\n\nthat with Him lies the second genesis,\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَغْنٰى وَ اَقْنٰىۙ‏(48)\n\nthat it is He who enriches and grants possessions,\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ رَبُّ الشِّعْرٰىۙ‏(49)\n\nthat it is He who is the Lord of Sirius;\nوَاَنَّهٗۤ اَهْلَكَ عَادَا۟ اۨلْٮئُوْلٰى ۙ‏(50)\n\nthat it is He who destroyed the former ‘Ad,\nوَثَمُوْدَا۟ فَمَاۤ اَبْقٰىۙ‏(51)\n\nand Thamud, sparing none [of them];\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا هُمْ اَظْلَمَ وَاَطْغٰىؕ‏(52)\n\nand the people of Noah before that; indeed they were more unjust and rebellious;\nوَالْمُؤْتَفِكَةَ اَهْوٰىۙ‏(53)\n\nand He overthrew the town that was overturned,\nفَغَشّٰٮهَا مَا غَشّٰى‌ۚ‏(54)\n\ncovering it with what covered it.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكَ تَتَمَارٰى‏(55)\n\nThen which of the bounties of your Lord will you dispute?\nهٰذَا نَذِيْرٌ مِّنَ النُّذُرِ الْاُوْلٰٓى‏(56)\n\nThis is a warner, [in the tradition] of the warners of old.\nاَزِفَتِ الْاٰزِفَةُ‌ۚ‏(57)\n\nThe Imminent [Hour] is near at hand.\nلَيْسَ لَهَا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ كَاشِفَةٌ ؕ‏(58)\n\nThere is none who may unveil it besides Allah.\nاَفَمِنْ هٰذَا الْحَدِيْثِ تَعْجَبُوْنَۙ‏(59)\n\nWill you then wonder at this discourse,\nوَتَضْحَكُوْنَ وَلَا تَبْكُوْنَۙ‏(60)\n\nand laugh and not weep,\nوَاَنْتُمْ سٰمِدُوْنَ‏(61)\n\nwhile you remain heedless?!\nفَاسْجُدُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَاعْبُدُوْا ۩‏(62)\n\nSo prostrate yourselves to Allah and worship Him!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Najm (The Star)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 26 verses. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of believers and sinners combined. The reciter will lead a respectable and honourable life and people will love and respect him.\nWriting this Surah and keeping it at a talisman makes one courageous in front of the ruler and makes the ruler respect him. He also comes out victorious in debates and discussions."
